This project is for create Autodesk Revit Addin using Revit C# API.

# Development guidelines:

## If create new functionality, refer to [project_structure.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/project_structure.mdc).

## If need to save or load data to local machine, refer to [local_storage.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/local_storage.mdc).

## If need to create wpf view for user interaction, refer to [wpf.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/wpf.mdc).

## For non-Revit API code, write code that can run both on .NET 8.0 and .NET Framework 4.8.

## If need to add package, add directly to csproj file, don't run dotnet command to try adding package.

## If need to create Revit parameter, refer to [revit_utils.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/revit_utils.mdc)

## If package run on .NET Framework 4.8 but not .NET 8.0, add condition to PackageReference in csproj definition, example:
```xml
<PackageReference Include="System.Net.Http" Version="4.3.4" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net48'" />
```

- Actively add debug log to execute process to help debug easier.
- Make sure all Revit API calls happened in valid Revit context to avoid "Revit API running out of context" errors.

## Making code work with multiple revit API version according to this guide:

- To support the latest APIs in legacy Revit versions:
```csharp
#if REVIT2021_OR_GREATER
    UnitUtils.ConvertFromInternalUnits(69, UnitTypeId.Millimeters);
#else
    UnitUtils.ConvertFromInternalUnits(69, DisplayUnitType.DUT_MILLIMETERS);
#endif
```

- "#if REVIT2021_OR_GREATER" сompiles a block of code for Revit versions 21, 22, 23 and greater.

To support removed APIs in newer versions of Revit, you can invert the constant:

```csharp
#if !REVIT2023_OR_GREATER
    var builtinCategory = (BuiltInCategory) category.Id.IntegerValue;
#endif
```
- "#if !REVIT2023_OR_GREATER" сompiles a block of code for Revit versions 22, 21, 20 and lower.

But only support for Revit version 2021 or higher.

Remember: Call within valid Revit context using ExternalEvent pattern!
